 "text": "A planxty is a folklore motif. The music of the Otherworld was more beautiful than anything in our world. The Irish harper Turlough O'Carolan slept on a fairy mound and awoke a musical genius. He coined the word planxty for the quality and shape of fairy music. It was not regular or rhythmic, but its odd harmony cast a hypnotic and yearning trance.",
